**Verdict:** trust intact, value high, recommendation revise, 0 blockers, 2 concerns.

**Strongest hit:** The closing callback — mother's posters into the music, sister into the video and a song about absence — is built entirely from completed facts, so it reads exactly as well in a year as today, and the Type 3/Type 4 hedging throughout means new evidence can only sharpen the piece, never falsify it.

**Highest-priority concern:** The "PRIMA is a rank" section's tour line ("is scheduled to open September 9, 2026... describes it as sold out") is the one place present tense breaks the piece's otherwise disciplined dated-past-tense style — a reader in September 2027 will hit it as a small, localized "wait, is this stale?" jolt. Minimum fix: past tense with a publication-date anchor on the next refresh pass.
